WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.900
Wrath of the Black Manta, for every crime there is punishment, for every vice there is vengeance.

00:00:23.820 --> 00:00:32.220
And welcome to NEStalgia, a chronological exploration of every NES game released in North America.

00:00:32.600 --> 00:00:34.060
I'm Mike. I'm Sean.

00:00:34.440 --> 00:00:35.320
And I'm Joe.

00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:36.780
Is that true?

00:00:36.780 --> 00:00:38.940
For every vice there is vengeance?

00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:40.320
Do you agree with that statement?

00:00:40.460 --> 00:00:42.060
Yeah. What do they mean by vice?

00:00:42.200 --> 00:00:44.140
I mean, there could be vices that aren't like criminal.

00:00:44.440 --> 00:00:51.520
Well, I think what it means by that is like this is basically a playable like dare PSA.

00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:56.120
And the vice is anything to do with recreational drug.

00:00:56.520 --> 00:01:03.840
Yeah, because in the game you are trying to take down DRAT, I believe it, the D-R-A-T, DRAT,

00:01:03.840 --> 00:01:06.940
DRUG RUNNERS AND TERRORIST ASSOCIATION.

00:01:07.120 --> 00:01:09.560
Yeah. And there's a lot of drugs in this game.

00:01:10.600 --> 00:01:12.420
Yeah. Specific drugs, too.

00:01:12.840 --> 00:01:16.620
I mean, surprisingly, they like, yeah, they call out specific, like dope.

00:01:17.540 --> 00:01:20.600
I feel like normally if it's like a kid's PSA thing, they would just say drugs.

00:01:20.600 --> 00:01:25.400
Yeah, it does feel like the terrorist thing is just like an additional like scary word,

00:01:25.580 --> 00:01:29.260
right? And I don't really recall too many terrorists in the game.

00:01:29.460 --> 00:01:34.740
Definitely a lot of would-be child kidnappers, though, because that's another story plot point,

00:01:34.880 --> 00:01:40.240
is that children in New York specifically, hyper-localized to New York, are being kidnapped.

00:01:40.240 --> 00:01:47.620
And your sensei, you're the black manta, your sensei alerts you about this situation because

00:01:47.620 --> 00:01:50.640
one of his students has also been kidnapped.

00:01:51.060 --> 00:01:55.440
And that's what persuades the black manta to stop all these kidnappings.

00:01:55.600 --> 00:01:57.180
And I have two questions about that.

00:01:57.340 --> 00:01:59.260
Is this really a job for a ninja?

00:02:01.140 --> 00:02:05.580
And if it is, why didn't he always just do this, right?

00:02:05.580 --> 00:02:09.840
And if he always had the capability to stop children from being kidnapped, shouldn't he

00:02:09.840 --> 00:02:11.340
have just agreed anyway?

00:02:11.580 --> 00:02:12.880
Oh, no, Taro wasn't in trouble.

00:02:13.200 --> 00:02:14.080
Okay, here's the thing.

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:21.260
So, first of all, he didn't know until he was called by his sensei.

00:02:21.740 --> 00:02:29.380
Before his sensei called him, he was just sitting in a dark room in full ninja garb, which I

00:02:29.380 --> 00:02:31.760
imagine he spends most nights doing.

00:02:31.760 --> 00:02:36.640
So, you know, if Batman doesn't know about a crime, how is he going to stop it?

00:02:38.180 --> 00:02:47.760
And secondly, since it seems that this organization of terrorists and drug runners is primarily

00:02:50.120 --> 00:02:58.760
staffed by ninjas or other martial artists, then one would assume that there are other ninjas

00:02:58.760 --> 00:03:00.840
that, you know, maybe free agents.

00:03:00.840 --> 00:03:10.280
Hmm. Well, so what he should have done is when the sensei said kids are being kidnapped, but

00:03:10.280 --> 00:03:16.480
before he said Taro has also been kidnapped, the Black Manta should have said, stop right

00:03:16.480 --> 00:03:17.800
there. I'm going to go right now.

00:03:17.940 --> 00:03:19.120
I don't care who else has been kidnapped.

00:03:19.220 --> 00:03:21.040
If one person's been kidnapped, I'm going.

00:03:21.300 --> 00:03:23.540
You cannot interrupt your sensei.

00:03:23.700 --> 00:03:24.640
Oh, I forgot.

00:03:24.680 --> 00:03:27.620
I forgot the sensei-sensei relationship.

00:03:27.620 --> 00:03:31.320
And Black Manta's kind of like a ninja with attitude, right?

00:03:31.440 --> 00:03:35.380
Like, what's up with that main menu where he's posing for his rap album cover?

00:03:36.820 --> 00:03:41.980
It's funny that you say that because anytime, like, there's a cut scene and it shows, like,

00:03:42.100 --> 00:03:49.640
closer to the Black Manta's face, like, I just can't not visualize sort of, like, a pudgy

00:03:49.640 --> 00:03:56.020
dad. Like, a pudgy blonde dad wearing this ninja costume.

00:03:56.260 --> 00:04:01.340
Like, there's something in his eyes that just shows him that, like, he's past his prime or

00:04:01.340 --> 00:04:04.660
maybe he's still not really in shape enough to do this.

00:04:04.780 --> 00:04:06.500
But, I don't know.

00:04:06.580 --> 00:04:08.020
That's sort of the vibe I was getting.

00:04:08.400 --> 00:04:14.140
I mean, is that the, like, because of the, like, don't do drugs kids, like, after school

00:04:14.140 --> 00:04:19.600
kind of message here that you associate that with that kind of person?

00:04:19.780 --> 00:04:20.620
It might be.

00:04:20.840 --> 00:04:26.980
I, it could be something completely, uh, pathological.

00:04:27.320 --> 00:04:35.000
I don't know. Yeah, the Black Manta's the dad and the sensei is the grandfather and Taro's just getting one

00:04:35.000 --> 00:04:37.980
really expensive lesson on why you don't do drugs.

00:04:38.120 --> 00:04:39.600
Like, everyone else is in on it.

00:04:39.600 --> 00:04:42.240
That's why you always leave a note.

00:04:42.620 --> 00:04:44.240
Right, exactly. Thank you, Sean.

00:04:44.360 --> 00:04:46.680
You got it. A lot of notes. Uh, yeah.

00:04:46.860 --> 00:04:50.600
And also, while we're on the subject of plot, I swear we'll talk about the game at one point.

00:04:50.780 --> 00:04:52.840
Um, the children you save.

00:04:53.040 --> 00:04:55.220
Can we talk about these so-called children?

00:04:56.360 --> 00:05:03.640
Yeah. Yeah, this is definitely, um, at some point not intended to be children and then was rewritten

00:05:03.640 --> 00:05:07.260
to be children because these sprites do not look like children.

00:05:07.260 --> 00:05:17.900
Yeah, there's, there's like a whole, a very diverse array of, of ages and races and genders.

00:05:17.900 --> 00:05:25.400
Like, at one point, I, um, I, I picked up, you know, I, I rescued somebody and they're

00:05:25.400 --> 00:05:26.800
like, hey, my friend's next door.

00:05:26.960 --> 00:05:28.540
Can you, can you go rescue them?

00:05:29.500 --> 00:05:31.160
And we're like, yep, sure.

00:05:31.300 --> 00:05:32.640
Say no more. I'll go get them.

00:05:32.640 --> 00:05:37.040
Um, and then you go next door and you rescue the same exact person.

00:05:37.520 --> 00:05:45.460
Um, and, and, an old lady and your character is just like, yeah, your buddy, he, he said

00:05:45.460 --> 00:05:46.320
you were in here.

00:05:46.560 --> 00:05:47.800
So I came and gotcha.

00:05:47.820 --> 00:05:53.280
And, and I just feel like, you know, everything was written before they actually, you know,

00:05:53.520 --> 00:05:55.740
created the art assets for this game.

00:05:57.380 --> 00:05:59.140
See, I, yeah, I almost feel like it's gotta be the opposite.

00:05:59.220 --> 00:06:02.140
They created the art assets and then they were like, oh, we should have made them kids.

00:06:02.280 --> 00:06:03.580
And we can just say they're kids.

00:06:05.440 --> 00:06:12.660
Yeah. And what good is a, any kind of ninja video game if it's not, uh, you know, full of awesome

00:06:12.660 --> 00:06:18.840
ninja arts and cool moves and, uh, you know, like a ninja who feels really in control of

00:06:18.840 --> 00:06:19.720
his platforming.

00:06:19.940 --> 00:06:26.780
How is the Black Manta, you know, just his movement, his weapon options, his melee combat,

00:06:27.240 --> 00:06:30.920
you know, compare it for me to Ryu from Ninja Gaiden, if you will.

00:06:30.920 --> 00:06:39.440
If I'm thinking of Ryu, I mean, the movement here is worse, but like, it's totally, it's

00:06:39.440 --> 00:06:42.480
weird because the whole time, like, this is totally, like, I, I didn't have a hard time

00:06:42.480 --> 00:06:43.920
with it. It wasn't frustrating or anything.

00:06:44.120 --> 00:06:50.520
I think that I just have that feeling from Ninja Gaiden in my head when I'm playing a game

00:06:50.520 --> 00:06:56.080
like this. So like, it is noticeable that it, that it's not at that level, but it's, I will say, I

00:06:56.080 --> 00:07:02.360
think the movement is better than like 75% of platformers we've played on, on the NES,

00:07:03.040 --> 00:07:07.840
but it just doesn't, it doesn't stand out as like, as top, you know, like, like there's

00:07:07.840 --> 00:07:09.220
plenty of room for improvement.

00:07:09.880 --> 00:07:17.060
Yeah. I'd say that this is a, the, the people that designed movement and controls for this game,

00:07:17.180 --> 00:07:23.480
I'd say that they were kind of forward thinking because there, there's like one attack button,

00:07:23.480 --> 00:07:26.220
um, and it's completely context based.

00:07:26.440 --> 00:07:30.040
Like if you're right next to a guy, you're going to slash at them.

00:07:30.420 --> 00:07:33.920
And if there isn't a guy right in front of you, you're just going to shoot your star.

00:07:34.560 --> 00:07:40.300
And then you have the like holding down to charge of your special, special attacks.

00:07:40.500 --> 00:07:46.020
That is, is still kind of, uh, is kind of like a new concept right now.

00:07:46.200 --> 00:07:51.980
Um, with that, I thought that was pretty satisfying, but it seems to be in the movement itself,

00:07:51.980 --> 00:07:57.580
while like the difference in like the heights of, of jumping to the side or like somersaulting

00:07:57.580 --> 00:08:03.160
or just jumping straight up can be kind of weird to, uh, to modulate.

00:08:03.840 --> 00:08:12.060
Um, it seemed to be thinking about the quality of life of the player more than the average

00:08:12.060 --> 00:08:14.860
game, which is more like, fuck you.

00:08:15.140 --> 00:08:16.600
The button is the button.

00:08:17.360 --> 00:08:23.420
Yeah. And, and, and it's adding onto the, uh, that holding down the button for your power up move,

00:08:23.580 --> 00:08:28.140
just holding down the button plus one direction on the directional D pad, giving you a different

00:08:28.140 --> 00:08:29.520
move than like another direction.

00:08:29.920 --> 00:08:32.060
That's, you know, that's very like super smash brothers.

00:08:32.120 --> 00:08:35.520
Like it's cool because it, that gives you a lot more options.

00:08:36.520 --> 00:08:41.620
Really getting all of the, uh, getting the most out of that two button controller.

00:08:42.080 --> 00:08:49.800
Yeah. I, I think that overall though, like circling back to your question, Mike, what, what I

00:08:49.800 --> 00:08:53.160
think could have been better about the movement is even though it's like, it's totally fine,

00:08:53.260 --> 00:08:56.060
totally passable. I don't feel like a ninja, you know?

00:08:56.280 --> 00:09:01.220
Yes. I feel like I'm controlling a good game, but I don't feel like, don't get that feeling

00:09:01.220 --> 00:09:05.980
that Ninja Gaiden gave me where I'm like, oh, the, the motion makes me feel like a swift

00:09:05.980 --> 00:09:07.080
ninja. Right.

00:09:07.260 --> 00:09:10.820
And I don't know if that's just because he doesn't like when he jumps in the air, he

00:09:10.820 --> 00:09:16.220
grabs his knees and starts doing like a, you know, flip in the air each time he jumps or

00:09:16.220 --> 00:09:21.900
something. Like, I don't know if it's an animation thing, but yes, it does feel more like he is in a

00:09:21.900 --> 00:09:26.460
beat them up than he is in, in a platformer or action kind of game.

00:09:26.580 --> 00:09:29.140
I think it's mostly just the speed of movement in general.

00:09:29.320 --> 00:09:31.760
Like you, cause that is the pace in which he walks.

00:09:31.760 --> 00:09:36.840
If you were playing double dragon and not so much Ninja Gaiden, which is much faster

00:09:36.840 --> 00:09:39.620
and like, he's not doing like a ninja run.

00:09:39.620 --> 00:09:42.560
He's just sort of plotting towards the dudes.

00:09:43.120 --> 00:09:48.640
So, I mean, I, I said that like, oh, it's kind of forward, forward thinking in terms of

00:09:48.640 --> 00:09:53.800
design. It's just not forward thinking in terms of like what the game should be going for.

00:09:54.300 --> 00:09:59.160
Yeah. But I do think you touched on something that not a lot of people while playing would

00:09:59.160 --> 00:10:00.080
recognize, Sean.

00:10:00.320 --> 00:10:06.000
Um, and that is the, the situational context, contextual, uh, attack scheme.

00:10:06.200 --> 00:10:12.480
And then Joe, you touched upon the Ninja arts being assigned to, uh, the B button plus specific

00:10:12.480 --> 00:10:16.500
directions. And that is, that is great.

00:10:16.780 --> 00:10:21.580
And the Ninja arts themselves are, are interesting and you learn new ones as you go on, which is

00:10:21.580 --> 00:10:22.640
great for progression.

00:10:23.140 --> 00:10:24.720
Two things about the Ninja arts.

00:10:25.260 --> 00:10:29.480
The first being the convoluted method to use those Ninja arts.

00:10:29.560 --> 00:10:31.660
And I don't mean in the actual level to level thing.

00:10:31.760 --> 00:10:35.720
I mean, understanding that you're choosing them while you're doing it in the menus.

00:10:35.720 --> 00:10:39.360
That was a little like tough for me to understand.

00:10:39.360 --> 00:10:43.020
And I'm not sure if you guys agree with that or not, but I wasn't understanding that I

00:10:43.020 --> 00:10:48.340
was assigning Ninja arts to buttons, uh, in that little screen before the stage.

00:10:48.540 --> 00:10:52.880
The only reason that I did know is because this was one of the rare instances in which

00:10:52.880 --> 00:10:54.180
I did read the manual.

00:10:54.540 --> 00:10:58.420
I, I realized what was, what it wanted me to do.

00:10:58.660 --> 00:11:05.840
And it did take me a second to like figure out how to like get into switching them up.

00:11:05.920 --> 00:11:10.340
Like at first I thought it was just telling me, okay, this button does this, this button

00:11:10.340 --> 00:11:14.740
does that. But then eventually I realized that you can like go in and swap things out and maybe I

00:11:14.740 --> 00:11:16.300
didn't, maybe you have to, I can't remember.

00:11:16.480 --> 00:11:20.200
You have to, you have to earn a new one before you're able to swap anything or do you already

00:11:20.200 --> 00:11:22.480
have the option to swap early on?

00:11:23.020 --> 00:11:27.380
I, I actually didn't even realize that I could swap mid-level until very late.

00:11:27.380 --> 00:11:28.220
So I don't know.

00:11:28.360 --> 00:11:29.560
Oh, you can swap mid-level?

00:11:29.740 --> 00:11:30.700
I didn't know that until right now.

00:11:30.920 --> 00:11:31.860
Yes, you can. Oh, okay.

00:11:31.920 --> 00:11:38.480
Well, I had no idea. But at the beginning of the level, um, I didn't realize that you could, that you could do that.

00:11:38.560 --> 00:11:42.540
But once I figured, once I like just figured it out, once I got used to it, I thought it

00:11:42.540 --> 00:11:43.860
was a very good method.

00:11:44.020 --> 00:11:47.060
Granted, maybe it was more convoluted than I thought because I had no idea you could swap

00:11:47.060 --> 00:11:49.660
mid-level. I thought I was locked into my choices at the beginning of the level.

00:11:49.660 --> 00:11:56.360
Well, after each level, you're, you unlock a couple and then that would be at least for

00:11:56.360 --> 00:12:01.660
the first couple levels, your only real reason to do that is because you unlocked one.

00:12:01.840 --> 00:12:04.400
So I can understand where you'd get that vibe.

00:12:04.580 --> 00:12:05.460
Oh yeah. Yeah.

00:12:05.520 --> 00:12:07.360
But how do you do it in the middle of a level?

00:12:07.460 --> 00:12:09.760
Cause pausing doesn't, I think it just select.

00:12:10.880 --> 00:12:15.100
Really? I tried select just to see what, if it would do anything and it didn't, nothing happened.

00:12:15.240 --> 00:12:19.420
Yeah. If you press the select button during gameplay, it will show you the Ninja art screen.

00:12:19.660 --> 00:12:25.700
The more, you know, anyway, go, my other thing about the Ninja arts is they're a little

00:12:25.700 --> 00:12:31.340
like, uh, you know, not overpowered or whatever, but there isn't necessarily a limit to them

00:12:31.340 --> 00:12:33.100
or a magic meter or anything.

00:12:33.100 --> 00:12:36.860
And so you kind of just like should always be using them, right?

00:12:37.420 --> 00:12:43.720
Yeah. I guess the only limitation is just the time it takes to actually pull it off.

00:12:43.760 --> 00:12:48.540
And there are times where there are, I mean, not really.

00:12:48.540 --> 00:12:50.840
This is actually a pretty slow moving game.

00:12:50.980 --> 00:12:52.140
You never really get overwhelmed.

00:12:52.660 --> 00:12:55.780
There's only like one or two or three enemies on the screen at a time.

00:12:56.000 --> 00:12:58.620
So you, you'll kind of always have time to pull one off.

00:12:58.700 --> 00:13:04.400
So I'm a sort of arguing against my argument, but I guess that would be the trade-off if

00:13:04.400 --> 00:13:05.500
this were a harder game.

00:13:06.540 --> 00:13:12.100
Well, I, I do agree that like a lot of these are powerful and interesting, but I don't

00:13:12.100 --> 00:13:16.060
know why, but like in the moment to moment gameplay, I really never found them particularly

00:13:16.060 --> 00:13:18.260
useful except for some certain scenarios.

00:13:18.260 --> 00:13:22.740
You know, there's not a lot of times where you run, where you run into enemies that take

00:13:22.740 --> 00:13:25.180
more than one hit. It's really towards like the later levels.

00:13:25.280 --> 00:13:28.860
Once in a while you run into those like goblin looking people or like you run into those guys

00:13:28.860 --> 00:13:32.540
that are like flying on like kites and like they take a couple of hits.

00:13:32.540 --> 00:13:35.380
But for the most part, they all just look like Deadpool to me.

00:13:36.400 --> 00:13:42.520
Yeah. For the most part, you're, you're just fighting like regular people that take one hit to kill.

00:13:42.740 --> 00:13:47.600
And I just always, almost always found it just easier to just throw a star or whatever

00:13:47.600 --> 00:13:52.660
it is you're shooting at them or whatever, uh, rather than charge up a power up.

00:13:52.660 --> 00:13:54.600
I use the power us mostly on bosses.

00:13:55.200 --> 00:13:59.340
Um, and even then I think that I, it was kind of sparing.

00:13:59.480 --> 00:14:02.420
Like I, I wish that there, I had more of a reason to use them.

00:14:02.540 --> 00:14:05.300
And maybe that was because of like the charge up.

00:14:05.540 --> 00:14:09.320
Like I just felt like it was easier to shoot and then jump away from an enemy rather than

00:14:09.320 --> 00:14:10.580
like try and charge up.

00:14:10.680 --> 00:14:13.580
Granted, you don't have to charge it up all the way to fire it, but just something about

00:14:13.580 --> 00:14:16.620
it. I didn't feel the need to use the power ups that often.

00:14:16.780 --> 00:14:19.900
Like I would test them at the beginning of the level and then just not really use them

00:14:19.900 --> 00:14:26.660
the rest of the time. Joe, your comment about not feeling the need to use the ninja arts kind of leads to something

00:14:26.660 --> 00:14:30.460
that, uh, I wrote down in my notes and I just don't have an elegant way of saying

00:14:30.460 --> 00:14:36.380
it, but I wrote down the limited option, the limited option of gameplay outcomes.

00:14:36.380 --> 00:14:41.460
And what I meant by that is really that for the most part, every enemy you encounter in

00:14:41.460 --> 00:14:44.960
the game is shooting at you or punching at you.

00:14:44.960 --> 00:14:50.700
And they're either in a standing position that's at your level or a crouched position, uh, that

00:14:50.700 --> 00:14:52.840
you will then have to like jump over that.

00:14:52.980 --> 00:14:57.700
And I, and I don't know why I felt it in this game more than in other games where like, think

00:14:57.700 --> 00:15:00.300
about there's not that many outcomes in super Mario brothers, right?

00:15:00.300 --> 00:15:04.860
There's not as many projectile enemies and most enemies are just walking towards you.

00:15:04.940 --> 00:15:05.900
You have to jump over them.

00:15:06.040 --> 00:15:11.800
But in this game, it just felt like maybe because there's only two planes of battle, but it felt

00:15:11.800 --> 00:15:18.080
like each time I've encountered two new enemies or however many enemies at a time, it was just,

00:15:18.820 --> 00:15:24.300
I'm not actually able to think about like tactfully how I should take on these enemies.

00:15:24.480 --> 00:15:27.120
And instead it's just, uh, are they shooting on this plane?

00:15:27.260 --> 00:15:28.900
Then I should duck. Oh, are they ducking?

00:15:28.900 --> 00:15:29.740
I should jump.

00:15:30.000 --> 00:15:32.860
And you just like continually do that for a while.

00:15:32.860 --> 00:15:35.060
And it starts to, you start to feel it.

00:15:35.220 --> 00:15:40.000
And so I started using the Ninja Arch just to rejuvenate some of the gameplay and try something

00:15:40.000 --> 00:15:46.240
different, but yeah, they aren't really like, they're not needed and they're not like enhancing

00:15:46.240 --> 00:15:47.440
the gameplay in another way.

00:15:47.560 --> 00:15:52.380
Whereas, you know, just to go to the other Ninja game, Ninja Gaiden, like I do feel like,

00:15:52.500 --> 00:15:57.140
yeah, there's a lot of unfair enemies in that game, but you feel like you're more in control

00:15:57.140 --> 00:16:02.240
of your outcomes where in this game you really are just seeing where the enemy is positioning

00:16:02.240 --> 00:16:04.160
themselves and then just doing the opposite.

00:16:04.420 --> 00:16:08.680
You're kind of just doing like a game of rock, paper, scissors, but it's just you're always

00:16:08.680 --> 00:16:09.840
