They're not just like, oh, you know, like, that doesn't sound like it's for me.

00:48:14.780 --> 00:48:19.120
So if you haven't played Wrath of the Black Manta because you either never got around to

00:48:19.120 --> 00:48:23.620
it on its original run-through or whatever, I think we're all saying that it's worth the

00:48:23.620 --> 00:48:24.500
listener's time.

00:48:24.680 --> 00:48:28.780
But if this is your very first episode of Nostalgia, maybe check out some of the ones

00:48:28.780 --> 00:48:30.660
on the Essential Games list first before you think that we're just...

00:48:30.660 --> 00:48:32.360
No, no, check this out. It's very cool.

00:48:32.720 --> 00:48:34.040
We're just throwing everything out there.

00:48:34.120 --> 00:48:35.880
But, you know, who knows?

00:48:35.960 --> 00:48:40.540
Because we've been told that the Essential Games list isn't perfect, and I'm shocked to

00:48:40.540 --> 00:48:42.700
hear that. That just shocks me.

00:48:42.700 --> 00:48:46.920
Whenever we throw something essential, we should mention that we mean it'll be essential

00:48:46.920 --> 00:48:48.000
in 30 more years.

00:48:48.180 --> 00:48:51.460
So then everybody has to wait 30 years to tell us we're wrong about that, too.

00:48:51.700 --> 00:48:53.620
That's always the disclaimer, right?

00:48:54.380 --> 00:48:55.240
Right. I do.

00:48:55.380 --> 00:49:00.520
I like my Horizon Zero Dawn argument, and I'm going to listen to what the fans have to say

00:49:00.520 --> 00:49:06.920
about that. So if you think Horizon Zero Dawn is better than the other games I listed, keep in mind,

00:49:07.100 --> 00:49:09.100
that's kind of a tough competition.

00:49:09.100 --> 00:49:12.720
All right? It's not every day you get Mario Odyssey and Breath of the Wild in the same year.

00:49:12.880 --> 00:49:16.320
Unless you get Tears of the Kingdom and Super Mario Wonder in the same year.

00:49:16.420 --> 00:49:18.160
How do they keep doing this at Nintendo?

00:49:18.660 --> 00:49:20.940
Wild stuff. We're going to keep doing this, too.

00:49:21.340 --> 00:49:23.860
Next week, we have a game called Zexies.

00:49:24.060 --> 00:49:25.280
I think that's how you say it.

00:49:26.080 --> 00:49:27.260
Did you just call me Zexy?

00:49:27.440 --> 00:49:29.200
Yeah, I think I did. Thank you.
